  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nTemperatures will be hot today in most areas and in the east on\nSaturday with southwest flow over Montana and ridge over the \nnorthern plains. Highs today will be in the upper 90s in the \nsoutheast with RH in the teens. While the strongest winds today in\nthe southeast will before the lowest RH, winds are expected to be\nstrong enough this afternoon to have critical Fire Weather \nconditions over the southern half of Fire Weather 122 especially \nover Prairie, Dawson and Wibaux Counties. SE winds will be strong\nenough this morning to maintain the Lake Wind Advisory over Fort\nPeck Lake with the strongest winds over the eastern half of the\nlake.  \n\nA dry cold front moves across NE Montana tonight with somewhat\nlower temperatures on Saturday although some areas in the east\nwill have highs in the lower 90s. \n\nUpper low moves inland from the Pacific early next week. At the\nsame time, muggy airmass over the Midwest gets advected into\nMontana on easterly winds on Sunday. Look for chances for showers\nand thunderstorms in some areas on Sunday. Showers and \nthunderstorms will become widespread Sunday night and continue  \nMonday and Monday night. At this point, it looks like the rain\ndiminishes late Monday night and Tuesday as a dry slot moves into\nthe forecast area.\n\nWhile models and ensembles vary on how much precipitation will\noccur, they agree on the heaviest precipitation occurring near the\nCanadian Border and rainfall totals being lighter going south. The\nNBM probability for one inch or more rain between 12z Sunday and\n12z Tuesday varies from 80-90 percent along the Canadian Border to\n20 to 30 percent south of MT 200. \n\nWednesday and Thursday looks dry at this time with the upper\nlow/through off to the east. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nDeviations from NBM for today included lower RH given that\nThursday min RH south of the Yellowstone River was lower than\nexpected. Increase winds a few mph today. No deviations were made\nbeyond today. \n\nConfidence is HIGH in the hot temperatures and low RH especially\nsouth today. Confidence is high in the rain occurring Sunday night\nthrough Monday night but confidence is low on the rainfall\namounts.",
